<section class="c-page">
    
    
    <section class="c-container c-container--has-bg-color u-white-bg c-container--1200 c-container--center">

    
    <div class="c-container__wrap">

        
                
            <div class="c-container__blocks">
                <div class="o-grid o-grid--large" data-item-count="2">
                                            <div class="o-grid__cell u-2/3@desktop">
    <div class="c-col c-col-text-area c-col--has-bg-color u-white-bg c-content">
                    <p class="lead-p"><strong>Put on a headset. Enter a South Indian temple. Let a 2,000-year-old dance tradition guide you from the threshold to the inner sanctum.</strong></p>
<hr />
<p><strong>MargaM</strong> guides you through a virtual South Indian temple on a memorable journey through Bharatanatyam – one of the world’s oldest classical dance forms. Through a VR headset, you move from the temple’s entrance to its inner space encountering intricate moves, held inside an original soundscape of voice, music and song.</p>
<p>A first-of-its-kind project integrating Bharatanatyam into VR headsets MargaM is created by Dance artist <strong>Divya Kasturi</strong> in collaboration with leading digital technologists and partners. MargaM represents a bold meeting of ancient artistic tradition and pioneering technology.</p>
<p class="smaller-p"><strong>Collaborators</strong> Clémence Debaig (Unwired Dance), Rebecca Evans (Pell Ensemble), Samuel Lawrence (Samuel Lawrence Limited)</p>
<p class="smaller-p"><strong>Supporters/Partners</strong> Dr Leslie Deere, Dan Shorten, Guildhall Production Studio, Target 3D, artsdepot, Alyssa Mello, DKC is part of the Artist Residency Programme at the Centre for Performance, Technology, and Equity (PTEQ) at Royal School of Speech and Drama and Divya Kasturi is an Associates Programme Pilot Artist at Guildhall School of Music and Drama</p>
<p class="smaller-p">Arts Council England National Lottery Project Grants</p>
<p class="smaller-p">Header image © Divya Kasturi</p>
            </div>
</div>
                                            <div class="o-grid__cell u-1/3@desktop">
    <div class="c-col c-col-text-area c-col--has-bg-color u-east-green-bg c-content">
                    <p><strong>5 &#8211; 7 November 2026<br />
</strong></p>
<p><strong>The Dance Floor<br />
Sadler’s Wells East</strong></p>
<p><strong>Free<br />
For ages 12+</strong></p>
<p><a style="background-image: none;" href="https://www.sadlerswells.com/your-visit/sadlers-wells-east/welcome-to-sadlers-wells-east/"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class=" wp-image-33630 aligncenter" src="https://sadlers-wells-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2025/03/sw_east_primary_landscape_white_logo.png?fit=300%2C300&quot;" alt="Sadler's Wells East logo" width="150" height="41" /></a></p>
            </div>
